# Rasa Skills / Maestro (Telano)

This repo is a **calm_v2 / Maestro Skills** project. Do not introduce CALM v1
artifacts (`config.yml`, `domain.yml`, flow YAMLs under `data/`, classic
`credentials.yml`). Keep `endpoints.yml` as a thin platform file (NLG /
`model_groups` only) — never add classic `action_endpoint` / `actions_module`.

Scaffold new projects with `rasa init --engine maestro` (there is no
`--template voice`).

## First commands

```bash
make verify
make train
make inspect
```

Prefer `make` targets over raw `uv run rasa …`.

## Layout

- Root: `agent.yml`, `integrations.yml`, `endpoints.yml`, `memory.yml`, `responses.yml`
- One skill per folder under `skills/<id>/`
- Session opener: `skills/default_session_start/` (`execute_tool` then `utter_greet`)
- Local-first tools: `skills/<id>/tools.py` (auto-discovered)
- Shared tools only in `tools/*.py` via `import_tools`
- Demo backend in `lib/database.py` + `data/source/*.json`

## Tool authoring

- Single-skill tools → `skills/<name>/tools.py` (no `import_tools`)
- Shared / session-start tools → `tools/*.py` + `import_tools`
- Reference tools in plain prose (`Call run_speed_test`)
- `@` is only for `@skill.<id>` and `@block.<id>` — never `@tool.`
- Never name a tool the same as a skill (`factory_reset_router`, not `reset_router`)
- Declare every `context.memory.set` key in skill or project `memory.yml`
- Do not rely on the LLM to call zero-arg setup tools; load identity at session start

## Progressive control order

prose → `tool_constraints` → scoped `if:` → verbatim `utter:` → `ordered_block`

Showcase skill: `reset_router` (remote factory reset via `factory_reset_router`).

## Model / stack

- `rasa-pro==3.19.0.dev3` with uv prereleases
- LLM: `gpt-5.2` — do **not** set `temperature`
- Deepgram under `channels.inspector` in `integrations.yml`

## Secrets

Never commit `.env`. Document vars only in `.env.example`.
Makefile may `-include .env` for presence checks but must **not** `export` it.
